#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98d34774-ec2d-59a3-a2cc-a70ee850eb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277778} {:answer/id #uuid "0f3ab75e-f101-5f93-9447-26bba28956e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $2.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277779} {:answer/id #uuid "716831a6-3a2c-535b-b464-bfb88d474e55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100$ and $25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277780} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe099e2-26ab-52f1-827b-5edf3e83d6fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$50$ and $12.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277781} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d8b558-e408-5f5a-8a7d-7543f64857d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98d34774-ec2d-59a3-a2cc-a70ee850eb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277778} :answer-field/id #uuid "24cb62ba-b7a1-56fb-bbb4-e161804e0324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26228f75-ba8b-5cfd-bc2f-68ab172288f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-115135" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{100}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=100$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=100,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{100}=10.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=10,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 10=20,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdfa7b5b-5f9c-5e7b-a4a8-a96583b2c87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{12.25}+\\frac{y^2}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277785} {:answer/id #uuid "9048d640-b9d2-5409-80ff-6efc19ab7929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{3.5}+\\frac{y^2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdfa7b5b-5f9c-5e7b-a4a8-a96583b2c87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{12.25}+\\frac{y^2}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277785} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaa5418f-11d7-5cdc-8dcc-cdfa6cbefc32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca370114-02f2-595d-bf62-dcbcc65e8ed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-279151" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975339/assets/0f3972825271a2f9471657919ed3669c63e03cd3740a436ab14cc30ed65b73bc.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{7}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9129169a-f87a-542e-9904-9f49f7dea190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^2/9 + 4y^2/81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9129169a-f87a-542e-9904-9f49f7dea190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^2/9 + 4y^2/81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232877} :answer-field/id #uuid "e63fd335-6717-55c1-9b71-d77d090e8bc5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d11d0095-5740-5d82-8a0d-f23a175699b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279153" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975339/assets/b12eb6672d263655f9f77eaafbf486a7be5bf9b7673c73fd0d75382d192a658b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{3}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{81}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08980b73-d334-596a-bc9e-f3051da133a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277789} {:answer/id #uuid "670a1206-33d5-5c65-8523-b05f7ab90322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277790} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0e4552-0b48-510c-a14c-df5837f90218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277791} {:answer/id #uuid "d30a5299-90a5-5e3e-9559-f3b642b5e277" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277792} {:answer/id #uuid "380ebbfc-3200-568d-b014-505ec52b7350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08980b73-d334-596a-bc9e-f3051da133a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277789} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9da84a8-06dc-557e-a981-a8b198ff51f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9972b8aa-75a5-5aae-86c3-11647818e833" :question/math-academy-id "q-7595" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=16$ and ${b}^{2}=9.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=16,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be  $a=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=9,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b22326-a022-5ce9-8c8f-5b92d6ceb501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277796} {:answer/id #uuid "52bf4c3b-47fe-5a95-a6c2-285d65e8b473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277797} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9cd681-23f6-5056-8efd-fb7f503a8310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277798} {:answer/id #uuid "f67726da-c546-5c7e-a816-e6f448e62798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277799} {:answer/id #uuid "537c73db-17df-5790-81bb-c7aefd37b84c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d9cd681-23f6-5056-8efd-fb7f503a8310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277798} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f22fe96-8060-5b94-8510-e4d0d4c2dbd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33e8b3ba-6017-5a10-821d-5c72e377f3a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-7608" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975339/assets/202dec2a2e75aa6720181eb925f98999031453f8f1f8822dd86d7a2baab21396.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
